content:
{
  "asset": "Pump P-110 – AquaDyne HF-300 end-suction centrifugal pump, serial HF3-24020",
  "priority": "P1",
  "stop_equipment_now": true,
  "condition_assessment": [
    {
      "statement": "Drive-end bearing housing temperature is 92 C and rising. The HF-300 manual sets the limits as normal up to 70 C, alarm at 80 C and trip at 90 C, so the reading is 2 C above trip. The manual measures bearing temperature on the housing surface, so these limits apply directly to the reported reading. Stop the pump.",
      "citations": [
        "C02",
        "C01"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Vibration is 4.0 mm/s. Using Figure 3 (mm/s RMS on the bearing housings), this falls in Zone B (2.8–4.5 mm/s, 'Long-term operation'). That is below the 4.5 mm/s Zone C boundary ('Restricted - plan maintenance') and well below the 7.1 mm/s Zone D stop limit. Vibration alone would not require shutdown, but the temperature trip overrides it.",
      "citations": [
        "C07",
        "C06"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "The bearing is reported as noisy. The manual requires both bearings to be replaced as a pair when either shows wear, noise or high temperature. This bearing meets two of those criteria (noise and high temperature).",
      "citations": [
        "C10"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "probable_causes": [
    {
      "statement": "Drive-end bearing wear (most likely). It is consistent with both the noise and the high bearing temperature, and it is a listed cause of both high bearing temperature and vibration.",
      "citations": [
        "C09",
        "C10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Over-greasing of the bearing is a listed cause of high bearing temperature.",
      "citations": [
        "C09"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Shaft misalignment is a listed cause of both high bearing temperature and high vibration.",
      "citations": [
        "C09"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "tasks": [
    {
      "statement": "Stop pump P-110 immediately: the drive-end bearing housing (92 C) is above the 90 C trip limit.",
      "citations": [
        "C02"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Isolate and drain the pump.",
      "citations": [
        "C10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Before dismantling, check the bearing grease quantity, since over-greasing is a listed cause of high temperature.",
      "citations": [
        "C09"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Remove the back pull-out assembly (68 kg) using lifting equipment. The casing and pipework can stay in place.",
      "citations": [
        "C01",
        "C02",
        "C10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Replace both bearings as a pair: drive-end 6312-C3 (HF3-512) and non-drive-end 6310-C3 (HF3-510).",
      "citations": [
        "C10",
        "C05"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Inspect the impeller, as required by the high-vibration troubleshooting action.",
      "citations": [
        "C09"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "If the mechanical seal is disturbed or found damaged, replace it with cartridge seal HF3-450B, not HF3-450. HF3-450B is pre-set, so no sleeve measurement is needed. Tighten the seal gland nut to 30 Nm.",
      "citations": [
        "C13"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Inspect the shaft sleeve for scoring. Replace sleeve HF3-455 if scoring is deeper than 0.1 mm.",
      "citations": [
        "C10",
        "C13"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Reassemble using a new casing gasket HF3-120 and tighten fasteners to Table 5 of the manual. Seal gland nut torque is 30 Nm per SB-2026-014.",
      "citations": [
        "C05",
        "C10",
        "C13"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Laser-align the shaft, since the work moves the bearing housing. Tolerances: parallel offset 0.05 mm; angular 0.05 mm per 100 mm.",
      "citations": [
        "C10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Before restart, confirm Plan 11 seal flush from the pump discharge is available and never run the pump dry.",
      "citations": [
        "C02"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "After restart, check bearing housing temperature against the limits (normal ≤70 C, alarm 80 C, trip 90 C). Measure vibration on both bearing housings and classify the highest reading using Figure 3.",
      "citations": [
        "C02",
        "C06",
        "C07"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "parts": [
    {
      "part_number": "HF3-512",
      "description": "Drive-end bearing 6312-C3",
      "quantity": 1,
      "citations": [
        "C05",
        "C10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "part_number": "HF3-510",
      "description": "Non-drive-end bearing 6310-C3 (replaced as a pair with the drive-end bearing)",
      "quantity": 1,
      "citations": [
        "C05",
        "C10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "part_number": "HF3-120",
      "description": "Casing gasket (replace whenever the casing is opened)",
      "quantity": 1,
      "citations": [
        "C05"
      ]
    },
    {
      "part_number": "HF3-450B",
      "description": "Cartridge mechanical seal, contingency only (if the seal is disturbed or damaged); supersedes HF3-450 for serial HF3-22000 and above",
      "quantity": 1,
      "citations": [
        "C13"
      ]
    },
    {
      "part_number": "HF3-455",
      "description": "Shaft sleeve, contingency only (if scoring is deeper than 0.1 mm)",
      "quantity": 1,
      "citations": [
        "C13",
        "C05"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "safety_controls": [
    {
      "statement": "Stop the pump now: the bearing temperature is above the 90 C trip limit.",
      "citations": [
        "C02"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Isolate and drain the pump before any dismantling.",
      "citations": [
        "C10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Lifting equipment is required for the 68 kg back pull-out assembly.",
      "citations": [
        "C02"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Never run the pump dry. The seal flush is Plan 11 from the pump discharge.",
      "citations": [
        "C02"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "labour": [
    {
      "statement": "Bearing replacement (pair): 6.0 h with 2 technicians.",
      "citations": [
        "C12"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Laser alignment: 1.5 h with 1 technician.",
      "citations": [
        "C12"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Contingency – mechanical seal replacement, if required: 4.0 h with 2 technicians.",
      "citations": [
        "C12"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "source_conflicts": [
    {
      "statement": "The manual parts list and seal procedure (Table 5) specify component seal HF3-450. Service Bulletin SB-2026-014 (issued 14 March 2026) applies to HF-300 pumps from serial HF3-22000. It supersedes HF3-450 with cartridge seal HF3-450B, removes the need for sleeve measurement, and raises gland nut torque from 25 Nm to 30 Nm. P-110 is serial HF3-24020, which is above HF3-22000, so the bulletin applies. Use HF3-450B at 30 Nm; HF3-450 must not be fitted.",
      "citations": [
        "C05",
        "C10",
        "C13"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "open_questions": [
    "Table 5 (fastener torques) is not in the evidence. Bearing housing, impeller nut and casing fastener torques cannot be specified.",
    "The manual's bearing replacement section gives no step-by-step procedure, fitting method or lubrication details. It is also unclear whether bearing replacement requires removing the impeller and seal.",
    "Grease type and correct fill quantity are not given, so the over-greasing check cannot be done against a documented value.",
    "Lockout/isolation details are not documented (electrical isolation of the 55 kW, 400 V motor; suction/discharge valve isolation). Hot-surface handling at 92 C is also not covered.",
    "It is not confirmed that the 4.0 mm/s vibration reading is RMS velocity taken on the bearing housing, as Figure 3 assumes. It is also unknown whether it is the higher of the two housing readings.",
    "The rate of temperature rise and the time the pump ran above the 80 C alarm and 90 C trip are unknown. Any secondary damage to the shaft (HF3-300) is unassessed.",
    "Whether the seal is disturbed or damaged during bearing work cannot be known until dismantling, so the need for HF3-450B is unconfirmed."
  ]
}
